      "id": 322,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### Reading these logs\n\n**Loki logs about itself.** Its own container is normally the\nsingle largest source of lines here — mostly one `caller=metrics.go`\nentry per query served. Because those lines *quote the query text*,\nany search for \"error\" makes Loki log a line containing \"error\".\nEvery error panel therefore excludes `caller=metrics.go`; without\nit the dashboard inflates its own error count on each refresh.\nReal Loki errors (`level=error`, scheduler/frontend RPC failures)\nstill show.\n\n**Three log formats, one regex.** Spark uses log4j\n(`26/08/28 08:31:21 INFO ...`), Loki uses logfmt (`level=info ...`),\nAirflow uses bracketed lines with ANSI colour codes. There is no\ncommon parseable level field, so severity is matched on the words\nthemselves. It is accurate but not infallible — a line *about* an\nerror counts as one.\n\n**Known steady noise:**\n- `headlamp` — errors every ~12s exporting traces to an\n  `otel-collector` service that does not resolve.\n- `coredns` — a `[WARNING]` per lookup for an optional custom\n  config file that was never created. Harmless.\n- `spark-connect-server` — recurring\n  `Issue communicating with driver in heartbeater`.\n\n**Cardinality warning.** Every scheduled Spark run creates two new\n`app` and `job` label values (`...-20260828t033000` and its\n`-driver`). That is ~16 new streams a day, growing without bound.\nWorth relabelling to a stable pipeline name at the Promtail level.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Notes",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
